      <p>While the underlying mathematical equations (like Harris-Benedict) are public domain, the way we have engineered them into this specific web application is protected by copyright and intellectual property laws. You cannot copy our website, clone our design, or steal our articles and publish them on your own blog. We believe in fair use—if you want to quote a small snippet of an article and link back to us, we appreciate the love! But wholesale copying is strictly forbidden.</p>
